t a single defined position of the starting material, and this labelled substrate was then carried through precisely the conditions that had given the unexpected product. The carbon-13 label appeared at a different skeletal position in the unexpected product. Isotopic labels are randomly redistributed around the carbon framework during a Wagner-Meerwein rearrangement. The displacement of the label away from the site at which it was installed is itself evidence that the intended intermediate's skeleton reorganized under the reaction conditions, and it is this kind of positional bookkeeping on individual atoms, rather than any purity assay or formula determination taken on its own, that converts a plausible mechanistic story into a demonstrated one."
